# Video Game Console Emulation Engineering

This skill provides architectural guidance, debugging methodologies, and design standards for developing and contributing to **game console emulators** (e.g. Dolphin, RPCS3, PCSX2, Ryujinx, RetroArch, DuckStation) in modern C++20 and Rust.

---

## 🎯 When to Activate

* **CPU Emulation & JIT Compilation:** Authoring CPU instruction interpreters, register state machines, and Just-In-Time (JIT) dynamic binary re-compilers (x86_64, ARM64).
* **Memory Architecture (MMU):** Implementing memory-mapped I/O (MMIO), fastmem page tables, virtual address translation, memory mirroring, and DMA controllers.
* **Graphics & PPU Pipeline:** Emulating legacy fixed-function and programmable GPU pipelines using **Vulkan 1.3 / OpenGL**, handling texture format conversions, shader translation, and framebuffers.
* **Audio Synthesis (APU):** Emulating sound hardware (PCM buffers, FM synthesis, ADPCM decompression, audio rings).
* **Cycle-Accurate Timing:** Managing hardware interrupt scheduling (IRQs), scanlines, vertical blanking (VBLANK), and peripheral synchronization without audio crackle or desync.
* **Upstream Open-Source Contributions:** Investigating regression issues, writing unit tests, and optimizing hot paths in existing open-source emulator codebases.

